Generate 1 sabotage suggestion for an polymorphism task in javascript.

Language syntax reference:
JavaScript OOP:
- Class: class Animal { constructor(name) { this.name = name; } speak() { return this.name; } }
- Inheritance: class Dog extends Animal { constructor(name) { super(name); } }
- Private: use #field syntax or closures. Use #balance for private fields.
- Polymorphism: override methods in subclass, no keyword needed

Task prompt: In a game's battle system, different attack types calculate damage in unique ways. Your task is to implement `MeleeAttack` and `MagicAttack` classes, ensuring they correctly extend the base `Attack` class and override its `calculateDamage` method to reflect their specific damage modifiers.

Current code in the editor:
```
class Attack {
  constructor(name, baseDamage) {
    this.name = name;
    this.baseDamage = baseDamage;
  }

  calculateDamage() {
    return this.baseDamage;
  }
}

class MeleeAttack extends Attack {
  constructor(name, baseDamage, strength) {
    // TODO: Call the parent constructor with name and baseDamage
    this.strength = strength;
  }

  // TODO: Override the calculateDamage method
  // It should return the base damage plus the strength.
}

class MagicAttack extends Attack {
  constructor(name, baseDamage, intelligence) {
    // TODO: Call the parent constructor with name and baseDamage
    this.intelligence = intelligence;
  }

  // TODO: Override the calculateDamage method
  // It should return the base damage plus intelligence multiplied by 2.
}

// Test cases
const punch = new MeleeAttack("Punch", 10, 5);
const fireball = new MagicAttack("Fireball", 15, 7);

console.log(`${punch.name} deals: ${punch.calculateDamage()} damage.`);
console.log(`${fireball.name} deals: ${fireball.calculateDamage()} damage.`);
```

